Package: endogCopulaBayes
Type: Package
Title: Bayesian Gaussian Copula Endogeneity Correction
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R: c(
    person(given = "Ashwin", family = "Malshe", role = c("aut", "cre"),
    email = "ashwin@malshe.com"),
    person(given = "Rouven E.", family = "Haschka", role = c("ctb", "cph"),
    comment = "Author of the reference implementation that the sampler in this package is ported from"))
Description: Implements the Bayesian 'Gaussian copula' endogeneity correction
    of Haschka (2025) <doi:10.1111/obes.70023> via a Metropolis-within-Gibbs
    sampler, ported from that author's reference implementation and built on
    shared machinery in 'endogCopula'. The sampler jointly estimates the
    regression coefficients, the residual variance, the copula correlation
    matrix, and Dirichlet probability masses describing the marginal
    distributions of the regressors, and returns the full MCMC chain
    alongside a thinned posterior sample with print and summary methods.
